<<PlayBackgroundMusic Exciting_1>>
<<SetBGSprite "KohliwadaGround">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Smiling">>
CoachDev: Ramu, right?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Yes, sir.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Smiling">>
CoachDev: I run a small academy nearby in Matunga, and I've been watching your brother—ten years old?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Just turned.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Smiling">>
CoachDev: I could see that—the name is already traveling between overs, so who's been coaching him?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Our lane, sir—dawn near the handpump with chalk, rubber balls, this bat, and habits of eyes, feet, hands, timing, and temper.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Smiling">>
CoachDev: Not a bad syllabus. Where's he now?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: With the team sharing chai and the tiny trophy—I told him to listen more than he speaks.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Smiling">>
CoachDev: Good. Tell me about home. Schooling, parents, work shifts… I like to know the ground a boy is growing in.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Baba works nights at the rolling mill, Maa cleans high-rises morning and afternoon—we manage with what comes and keep Raju's homework before everything.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Smiling">>
CoachDev: Non-negotiable. And he listens?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: He has learned to—missing once is fine, missing manners isn't, because we don't let poverty steal our manners.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: Diet?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: We do what we can—bananas on match days, chana most evenings, milk when there's extra, and prize money goes to ground repairs then home needs.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: Gear?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Second-hand pads later, not now—our mochi fixes shoes, I sand the bat with brick, and we keep the face up because respect is free.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: You speak like a coach and a brother both. Any pressure from family to stop this and focus only on studies?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: We had that talk—they gave us three months that became fourteen, as long as marks don't fall and we don't borrow money.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: Paperwork—birth certificate, school ID, address proof?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: School ID and ration card, yes—birth certificate I can find, or we can get a duplicate from the ward office.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: We can help with that later if needed. You know why I'm asking.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: Because a boy's story matters more than a highlight reel.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: Exactly. Talent is loud, background is the volume knob—and when I see a boy who sees the ball early and his ego late, I ask questions.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Smiling">>
Ramu: He's steady, sir. Special happens to steady boys when the world looks away.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: I'd like to meet your parents. If your father is on the night shift, maybe now?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Excited">>
Ramu: He leaves after the eight-o'clock bell, and we can catch him before he goes—it's a small walk from here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: Good. Let's go while the dust is still on your shoes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Excited">>
Ramu: This way, sir—watch your step near the drain where the light fades faster.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Serious">>
CoachDev: I can see, and Ramu—whatever happens next, don't change the lane inside his head.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Excited">>
Ramu: Same bell, same breath. He'll stay Raju.

<<SetCharacterExpression "CoachDev" "Smiling">>
CoachDev: Then take me to the door that raised him.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<FadeToBlack>>
<<StopBackgroundMusic>>
<<wait 3>>

===